WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.168
-My next guest created, writes,

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:04.504
and stars
in the Emmy-nominated series

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:06.472
"A Black Lady Sketch Show."

00:00:06.472 --> 00:00:10.543
Season two premieres Friday
on HBO and HBO Max.

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:13.680
Everyone, please welcome
Robin Thede!

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:14.714
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:19.218
Yeah! Come on.
Welcome back!

00:00:19.218 --> 00:00:21.521
-Thank you so much.
Thank you so much.

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:24.523
I know today is a wild day,
in many ways.

00:00:24.523 --> 00:00:26.826
So, hey, to all my friends.
-Yeah.

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:28.328
-All The Roots over there.

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:30.763
Questlove hit some weird drum
riff when you were intro'ing me.

00:00:30.763 --> 00:00:33.433
Appreciate that.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:35.167
♪♪

00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:37.670
There it is.
-Yeah.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:41.174
Robin, I want to get into
all things sketch

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:43.943
and talk to you about your show,
but first,

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.645
I'd love to know your thoughts

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:49.182
and how are you processing
all this?

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:52.751
-I am yet to process everything,
I think.

00:00:52.751 --> 00:00:56.389
You know, I'm --
Today is not a day

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:58.891
that I'm ready to yet say
I'm hopeful.

00:00:58.891 --> 00:01:02.195
It's a day that we're getting
a sliver of justice

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:04.364
with the Derek Chauvin guilty

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:07.033
on all three counts case --
verdict.

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:12.372
But nothing will ever make it
right for George Floyd's family.

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:14.907
But, you know,
it was so interesting

00:01:14.907 --> 00:01:18.211
to hear you and Jane talking
about all of this.

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:20.913
And her years and years
of activism and service,

00:01:20.913 --> 00:01:22.915
and she's right --
we have a long way to go, right?

00:01:22.915 --> 00:01:27.120
But I truly hope
this can be a corner

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.256
that helps this country turn.
You know?

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:32.525
And that we start to dig in
and really do the hard work.

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:33.827
-Yeah. Me too.
-I really do.

00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:36.629
-Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:38.064
I want to talk to you about this

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:39.298
because last time you came on,

00:01:39.298 --> 00:01:40.833
we talked about
"A Black Lady Sketch Show,"

00:01:40.833 --> 00:01:43.769
and it went on to get three
Emmy nominations!

00:01:43.769 --> 00:01:48.574
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's major!

00:01:48.574 --> 00:01:50.410
And --
-What were they thinking?

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:52.144
What were they thinking?!
-No, come on, you're fantastic.

00:01:52.144 --> 00:01:55.247
-They checked the wrong box.
Oh, it was good times.

00:01:55.247 --> 00:01:58.751
-Robin, it's not just your cast
that's made up of Black women,

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:02.555
but your staff and your crew
are all Black women.

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:05.057
Can you explain why that's
important to you?

00:02:05.057 --> 00:02:07.560
-I love it so much.
You know, in our writers' room,

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.462
which is all Black women,
our cast is all Black women,

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:12.865
our directors, our editors,
we get to really have

00:02:12.865 --> 00:02:16.002
this amazing experience
of not having

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:18.838
to explain ourselves
before we do our jokes,

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:21.841
of not having to, you know --

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.109
You know, you don't have to say,

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:25.444
"Okay, there's this singer
named Patti LaBelle."

00:02:25.444 --> 00:02:26.846
It's like,
"Yeah, yeah, we know that."

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:29.982
[ Both laugh ]
So we get to just make

00:02:29.982 --> 00:02:33.019
these sort of free, magical,
joy-filled sketches.

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:35.721
And season two,
which comes out on Friday --

00:02:35.721 --> 00:02:37.390
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I know, by the way.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:39.492
-Yes! We're so excited.

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:41.727
It's full of all this
Black-lady joy.

00:02:41.727 --> 00:02:44.530
And I think that's what
we really need right now.

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:46.999
-Has this past year --
Obviously, it must have affected

00:02:46.999 --> 00:02:48.935
the writing on this show.

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:54.039
-For me, you know, we started
season two, two weeks after --

00:02:54.039 --> 00:02:55.374
just after I saw you last.

00:02:55.374 --> 00:02:58.611
Two weeks after that,
we started writing season two.

00:02:58.611 --> 00:03:00.547
And then, we were ready
to shoot in March,

00:03:00.547 --> 00:03:03.949
and five days before we were
going to shoot, March of 2020,

00:03:03.949 --> 00:03:05.784
we got shut down,
as the whole industry did.

00:03:05.784 --> 00:03:09.388
So, for me, it was like, "Okay.
Well, this is a time to reset.

00:03:09.388 --> 00:03:11.224
A time to relax."
I'm very busy,

00:03:11.224 --> 00:03:13.826
and all of a sudden,
I had nothing to do so --

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:16.629
I really became more of myself,
and I wanted to feature that

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:20.299
on this year's show
and on this season.

00:03:20.299 --> 00:03:23.303
So I would love to show you
some pictures of kind of

00:03:23.303 --> 00:03:26.272
how I incorporated that
in the show.

00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:28.507
-Yeah, explain --
-I first started out -- yeah.

00:03:28.507 --> 00:03:30.175
Do you have one of those?
Oh, okay. Yeah.

00:03:30.175 --> 00:03:33.446
-This is Selena?
-That's my actual hairline.

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:35.881
This is a wig.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.881 --> 00:03:37.317
But, you know,
during quarantine, I was like,

00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:39.686
"Let me just embrace
my natural hairline."

00:03:39.686 --> 00:03:42.555
So I did that.
-So that's your actual hairline?

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:45.057
Starts...
-Yeah, starts around here.

00:03:45.057 --> 00:03:47.159
-Yeah, okay, wow.
Amazing.

00:03:47.159 --> 00:03:48.961
How about this character?

00:03:48.961 --> 00:03:51.664
-Oh, yeah, this is Chris.

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:53.599
This is me when I don't shave.

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:55.467
And, you know, all of quarantine
I did not shave my facial hair.

00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:56.969
-Can you grow a beard?

00:03:56.969 --> 00:03:58.671
-Yeah, yeah, yeah,
it's very easy.

00:03:58.671 --> 00:04:02.408
It connects, too.
Mine goes all the way around.

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:06.645
I was really, really excited
to just embrace my natural self.

00:04:06.645 --> 00:04:09.282
And then, you know,
here's the thing.

00:04:09.282 --> 00:04:13.586
This is a little sensitive,
but I actually --

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:17.089
I actually don't --
I don't want to offend people

00:04:17.089 --> 00:04:18.424
with the size
of my actual boobs.

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:20.760
Like, this is all taped down.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:25.764
But normally, I have a gigantic
bosom that I did grow.

00:04:25.764 --> 00:04:29.168
Yeah, there it is!
That's just my natural --

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:32.104
-This is your natural --
This is you being you.

00:04:32.104 --> 00:04:35.140
So this season, you're
definitely being more you

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:37.209
in all of these
three characters.

00:04:37.209 --> 00:04:40.245
I saw, by the way,
the trailer for your show.

00:04:40.245 --> 00:04:42.281
It was on HBO
after something I was watching.

00:04:42.281 --> 00:04:44.616
And, honestly, this is --
if you get three

00:04:44.616 --> 00:04:47.186
Emmy nominations
for last season, get ready.

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:48.787
'Cause this looks great, pal.

00:04:48.787 --> 00:04:51.457
Congratulations on this.
It's really, really funny.

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:52.792
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:52.792 --> 00:04:54.993
-Thank you.
I'm so excited about it.

00:04:54.993 --> 00:04:56.962
It really is good.
In all seriousness --

00:04:56.962 --> 00:04:58.297
And it's so good to see you,
by the way.

00:04:58.297 --> 00:04:59.698
I'm so devastated
I'm not there with you guys.

00:04:59.698 --> 00:05:02.835
-I know.
-It's -- I-I-I miss you.

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:05.004
-I know.
I appreciate you coming on.

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:07.140
-Yes, of course.
But the season is --

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:09.441
If season one was here,
season two is --

00:05:09.441 --> 00:05:12.111
I mean, it's wild.
It's wild.

00:05:12.111 --> 00:05:14.546
We really do want people
to feel joyous and to be able

00:05:14.546 --> 00:05:17.082
to take those 30 minutes
and really just turn off

00:05:17.082 --> 00:05:18.884
all the noise
of the outside world

00:05:18.884 --> 00:05:22.154
and just laugh
and feel that joy.

00:05:22.154 --> 00:05:25.324
-Yeah. I know
there's billboards all over --

00:05:25.324 --> 00:05:27.827
on buses and everything
here in New York.

00:05:27.827 --> 00:05:29.562
And you must be psyched
about that,

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:31.096
to see all the work
you put into it,

00:05:31.096 --> 00:05:33.065
and you go, "Yes!"
-I love it.

00:05:33.065 --> 00:05:34.767
So, yes.
On buses in New York,

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:38.471
we're getting pictures from
billboards all over the country.

00:05:38.471 --> 00:05:42.675
And then, I saw one
very disrespectful billboard

00:05:42.675 --> 00:05:45.745
where a tree was really
hating on the show.

00:05:45.745 --> 00:05:48.047
And it just said,
"A Lady Sketch Show,"

00:05:48.047 --> 00:05:50.116
which was very rude.
-Yeah.

00:05:50.116 --> 00:05:51.984
There you go, yeah.
So the tree blocked --

00:05:51.984 --> 00:05:54.020
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:55.521
-So, yeah,
that is disrespectful.

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:57.857
That tree should be removed.
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:57.857 --> 00:05:59.224
-And planted somewhere else,

00:05:59.224 --> 00:06:01.126
in front of
a different billboard.

00:06:01.126 --> 00:06:03.362
-Yeah! Exactly.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:03.362 --> 00:06:04.963
Go cover up
somebody else's show.

00:06:04.963 --> 00:06:07.066
Do you know how hard we worked?
-Yeah, come on, exactly.

00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:09.234
This is Robin Thede here.
Yeah.

00:06:09.234 --> 00:06:12.571
Pal, I want to show everyone
a clip from the show.

00:06:12.571 --> 00:06:14.606
Here's Robin Thede
in the new season of

00:06:14.606 --> 00:06:17.376
"A Black Lady Sketch Show."
Take a look.

00:06:17.376 --> 00:06:18.745
-Is everything okay, baby?

00:06:18.745 --> 00:06:20.279
-Yes.

00:06:20.279 --> 00:06:21.847
-Oh, my God.
You married Omarion?

00:06:21.847 --> 00:06:23.849
You knew he was my top choice!

00:06:23.849 --> 00:06:25.251
Wait a minute.
Omarion.

00:06:25.251 --> 00:06:26.919
Two kids.
Mansion.

00:06:26.919 --> 00:06:28.587
Don't tell me you a Video Vixen?
-Video Vixen.

00:06:28.587 --> 00:06:30.155
God dammit!
-Yeah.

00:06:30.155 --> 00:06:32.158
-[ Sobbing ]
Those were all my good choices.

00:06:32.158 --> 00:06:33.359
You stole my life!

00:06:33.359 --> 00:06:35.928
You were supposed to be with me,
Omarion!

00:06:35.928 --> 00:06:38.397
[ Energy crackling ]
Ohh.

00:06:38.397 --> 00:06:39.732
-Damn.
-Damn.

00:06:39.732 --> 00:06:41.133
[ Scoffs ]
You didn't think that

00:06:41.133 --> 00:06:43.102
you would be able to touch me,
did you?

00:06:43.102 --> 00:06:44.670
-[ Groans ]

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:46.339
-I know all about
your little MASH game,

00:06:46.339 --> 00:06:49.809
Selena Duplass from sixth grade,
and I'm thrilled to be in this

00:06:49.809 --> 00:06:53.746
paid-off house with this
perfectly symmetrical woman

00:06:53.746 --> 00:06:56.215
and our Rhodes Scholar children.

00:06:56.215 --> 00:06:58.717
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Robin Thede, everybody!

00:06:58.717 --> 00:07:01.320
Season two
of "A Black Lady Sketch Show"

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:05.024
premieres Friday
on HBO and HBO Max!

